Claude Code cloud sessions go through a GitHub proxy that rejects pushes of anything but a branch, so `tess sync` cannot push `refs/tess/sync` from there (ADR-0004). The idea on file: an inbox. A restricted session records its issue changes as events in a file on its own work branch (for example `.tess/inbox/<session>.json`), and the next local `tess sync` folds merged or fetched inboxes into the sync ref and clears them. Only the transport adapter knows ref names, so this touches `internal/sync/gitref` and the hook, not the merge. Deferred past loop 2 (design session, 2026-11-20): while the repo is private a cloud VM cannot install tess anyway. Revisit when a cloud session can run tess.